Your draft's frontmatter asserts a Wikipedia URL, and I verified it live: **the personal Wikipedia page is real and substantial** — 14 citations, full Early Life / Army / career / AMP / accolades sections. That's normally the entity-gap killer.

But the `-20` penalty requires Wikipedia **plus several authoritative dedicated biographies**, and the second half doesn't hold. Below Wikipedia, page one is TikTok, Facebook, YouTube, Tubi, two Fandom wikis, Famous Birthdays, a **soccer player named Duke Dennis**, and an unrelated professor at a Singapore university. The biography queries are owned by content farms — hamariweb, legit.ng, vocal.media ×3, thecityceleb, biographyhive, blessingsfusion, and a "forbesnetwork.co.uk" that is not Forbes.

